  "worked_solution": "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{\u2713}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,5=5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-15=5\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & \u2217\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-2=-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,6=-2\\cdot (-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$",
